@*
    Assurance Plans (BRD Part 2 Sec 8) -- Phase 2 Stage 3.

    Screen key : `org-assurance-plans`
    Group      : Organization Assurance
    Menu       : nav-assurance -> Assurance Plans (migration 091)
    Feature    : screen.org-assurance-plans
    Backend    :
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/plan-statuses
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/plan-types
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/plans?organizationId=&statusCode=&planType=&search=&page=&pageSize=
        POST   /practice/api/org-assurance/plans
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{id}?organizationId=
        DELETE /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{id}?organizationId=
        POST   /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{id}/{submit|approve|activate|close}
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{id}/items?organizationId=
        POST   /practice/api/org-assurance/plan-items
        DELETE /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{planId}/items/{itemId}?organizationId=
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/definitions?organizationId=&pageSize=200
        GET    /practice/api/organizations/{orgId}/employees

        POST   /practice/api/org-assurance/plans/{planId}/items/{itemId}/start-execution   (546)

    546 (2026-11-14, sir) -- BASIC PLAN FLOW
      A plan is made first; audits are added to it as slots (an audit may
      have many). Only Active audits are offered; slots change only while
      the plan is Draft or Submitted, inside the plan period (the API says
      why when not). Each slot shows its status -- Planned / In Progress /
      Completed / Not executed (audit retired, or plan closed) -- with its
      execution's code. Once the plan is Approved or Active, a Planned
      slot's 3-dot has Start Execution: the execution is created from the
      slot (origin PLAN, its dates, auditor as owner, team) and its scope
      is resolved then (545).
      Opened from Audit Definition's "Add to Plan" (encrypted navigation
      code, FilterType AuditDefinition), the page asks which Draft /
      Submitted plan to add the audit to -- or a new one -- and opens Add
      Item with the audit chosen; further Add Item clicks keep it chosen
      until the page is left.

    2026-11-14 (sir) -- ONE LIST, SLOTS AS CHILD ROWS
      The two panels (plans | items of the selected plan) are one full-
      width list of plans: Code, Name, Type, Period, Owner, Slots, Status.
      A plan's chevron -- or a click on its row -- opens its slots in a
      child row right under it (the Task Board's sub-task chevron); several
      plans can be open. The slots are read when the plan opens and again
      after any change to them; more than 20 show the first 20 and "Show
      all". "+ Add Item" sits under the slots while the plan is Draft or
      Submitted; Add Item is also on the plan's 3-dot. The selected-plan
      header, its Actions button and the Add Item button are gone (the
      plan's 3-dot holds the same items).

    552 (2026-11-14, sir) -- ENGAGEMENTS
      A plan's items are ENGAGEMENTS: who audits (auditor, team,
      department, branch), when (from / to) and WHICH audit definitions --
      one or more, picked in a dual list (Available / Selected, > < and
      up / down -- the Audit Configuration question set picker's layout,
      .oa-adopt-grid). Name defaults to the first audit's. "View Scope"
      (dialog link and the engagement's 3-dot) shows the selected audits'
      scope resolved NOW -- nothing is saved or frozen; the execution
      freezes it. The engagement rows show its code, name, audits and a
      rolled-up status (n / m audits done). Start Execution starts one
      execution per audit not yet started.

    566 (2026-11-16) -- AUDIT ENGAGEMENTS AS A RECORD (spec 4.5)
      The engagement form is shared with the Audit Engagements screen:
      Partials/_audit-engagement-form + js/Shared/audit-engagement-form.js
      (window.gracEngagementForm), in full view like the plan form. It adds
      the audit subject, objective, scope, auditee, instructions and the
      audit team (lead, members, reviewer, subject matter experts, external
      auditors, remarks). The dialog, the dual list, the auditor / branch /
      programme lists, View Scope and Start Execution moved there.

    554 (2026-11-14, sir) -- BRANCH AUDIT
      The engagement's Branch is a Location (GET scope-dimensions/BRANCH/
      values). With one, View Scope (and, since 555, the auditor's live scope
      and Freeze Scope in My Audits) keep only what is at that branch:
      practice instances linked to it in Operationalize, assets at it
      (departments and vendors as picked). Engagements saved before 554 keep
      their branch text, shown as "text only" (no narrowing).

    555 (2026-11-14, sir) -- MY AUDITS
      Start Execution creates the executions with a LIVE scope; they also
      start by themselves when the auditor opens My Audits on or after the
      From date. The auditor reviews, excludes (with a reason) and freezes
      the scope there.
      Backend (552): POST plan-items (+ engagementName, definitionIds[]);
      GET plans/{planId}/items/{itemId}/definitions;
      POST engagements/scope-preview.

    565 (2026-11-16, sir -- Audit Change spec 4.3, phase E) -- ANNUAL PLAN,
    PROGRAMMES, PLANNING METHODOLOGY
      Annual Audit Plan -> Audit Programmes -> Audit Engagements. The plan
      dialog gains Financial Year, Objectives, Planned Coverage, Budget
      (amount, currency), Planned Effort (days) and Resources. The plan
      list shows its programmes and planned vs actual (engagements, in
      progress, completed). A plan's child row lists its PROGRAMMES (code,
      programme, planning methodology, owner, planned vs actual); a
      programme row opens its ENGAGEMENTS under it (the engagement grid as
      before). Programmes are added / edited INLINE in the child row (no
      popups, sir): name, methodology (master, required), owner, order,
      objective. Every engagement belongs to a programme (the engagement
      dialog's Programme). An Approved / Active plan is REVISED (3-dot,
      with a reason): back to Draft, version + 1, the old values in the
      revision history shown in the child row; it is then re-submitted and
      re-approved.
      Backend: GET planning-methodologies; GET plans/{id}/programmes;
      POST plan-programmes; DELETE plans/{planId}/programmes/{id};
      POST plans/{id}/revise; GET plans/{id}/revisions.

    UX:
      * One plans list; a plan's programmes open under it, a programme's
        engagements under the programme.
      * 3-dots row menus (Edit / Delete / Submit / Approve / Activate /
        Close) driven by lifecycle status.
      * Dialog-based Add/Edit for both plans and items.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>@Model.Description</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="oaPlUnavailable" hidden>
    <div class="pm-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-days pm-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2 id="oaPlUnavailableTitle">Audit Plans are not available.</h2>
        <p id="oaPlUnavailableBody">Ask a GRAC Admin to enable this screen.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pm-panel" id="oaPlRoot" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar" style="flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
        <select id="oaPlFilterOrg"><option value="">Loading organizations...</option></select>
        <select id="oaPlFilterStatus"><option value="">All statuses</option></select>
        <select id="oaPlFilterType"><option value="">All types</option></select>
        <input id="oaPlSearch" type="text" placeholder="Search plan name / code..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaPlRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button primary" id="oaPlAddBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add Plan
        </button>
    </div>
    @* Audit & Assurance dashboard drill-down (414). *@
    <div id="oaPlDrillBanner" hidden></div>

    @* 2026-11-14 (sir): ONE full-width list of plans; a plan's slots open
       as a child row under it (the chevron, or a click on the plan row),
       instead of a plans panel beside an items panel. *@
    <div class="pm-table-wrap oa-pl-wrap" style="margin-top:12px;">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Code</th>
                    <th>Name</th>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>Period</th>
                    <th>Owner</th>
                    <th style="text-align:right;">Programmes</th>
                    <th>Engagements</th>
                    <th>Status</th>
                    <th></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="oaPlPlanBody">
                <tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load plans.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-pager" data-pager="oa-plans">
        <button class="pm-button" data-pg="prev" type="button">Previous</button>
        <span data-pg="label">Page 1</span>
        <button class="pm-button" data-pg="next" type="button">Next</button>
        <span data-pg="total" class="pm-pager-total">0 total</span>
    </div>
</section>

@* ---------- Plan dialog ----------
   2026-11-16 (sir): full view, fitting the master page -- the shared
   pm-dialog-fullpage (practice-management.css: beside the sidebar, below
   the topbar, the app chrome usable), opened with show(), not showModal(),
   as practice.js does for its full-page forms; the fields scroll inside. *@
<dialog id="oaPlPlanDialog" class="pm-dialog-fullpage">
    <form id="oaPlPlanForm" method="dialog">
        <div class="pm-dialog-heading">
            <h2 id="oaPlPlanDialogTitle">Add Plan</h2>
            <button class="pm-icon-button" type="button" id="oaPlPlanClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaPlPlanMessage" style="display:none;"></div>
        <input type="hidden" id="oaPlPlanEditId" />
        @* 2026-11-16 (sir): one 4-column grid, so the whole plan fits the
           full view without a scrollbar -- identity and period, name and
           owner, the annual figures, then the four texts side by side.
           minmax(0,1fr) so long option text can't force a horizontal
           scrollbar. The fields still scroll inside on a short window. *@
        <div class="oa-pl-plan-fields">
        <div class="oa-pl-plan-grid">
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Code <span class="required">*</span></span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanCode" type="text" maxlength="80" required />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Type <span class="required">*</span></span>
                <select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanType" required></select>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Period From</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanFrom" type="date" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Period To</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanTo" type="date" />
            </label>

            <label class="pm-field oa-pl-span-2">
                <span>Name <span class="required">*</span></span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanName" type="text" maxlength="240" required />
            </label>
            @* 121 hybrid role+employee Owner picker. *@
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Owner Role</span>
                <select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanOwnerRole" aria-label="Owner Role">
                    <option value="">Loading roles...</option>
                </select>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Owner</span>
                <select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanOwner" aria-label="Owner Employee (current holder)">
                    <option value="">-- pick a role first --</option>
                </select>
            </label>

            @* 565: the annual plan -- financial year, budget, effort (spec 4.3). *@
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Financial Year</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanFy" type="text" maxlength="40" placeholder="e.g. FY 2026-27" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Planned Budget</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanBudget" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Currency</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanCurrency" type="text" maxlength="10" placeholder="INR" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Planned Effort (days)</span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanEffort" type="number" min="0" step="0.5" />
            </label>

            @* 565: objectives, coverage, resources -- with the description.
               2026-11-16 (sir): each text on its own full-width row. *@
            <label class="pm-field oa-pl-span-all">
                <span>Objectives</span>
                <textarea class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanObjectives" rows="3" maxlength="8000"></textarea>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field oa-pl-span-all">
                <span>Planned Coverage</span>
                <textarea class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanCoverage" rows="3" maxlength="8000" placeholder="Units, processes, locations the plan covers"></textarea>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field oa-pl-span-all">
                <span>Resources</span>
                <textarea class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanResources" rows="3" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Auditors, co-sourced teams, tools"></textarea>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field oa-pl-span-all">
                <span>Description</span>
                <textarea class="pm-input" id="oaPlPlanDescription" rows="3" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
            </label>
        </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-dialog-actions">
            <button type="button" id="oaPlPlanCancel" class="pm-button">Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" id="oaPlPlanSubmit" class="pm-button primary">Save</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</dialog>

@* ---------- Engagement form + View Scope (566: shared with Audit
   Engagements; was the 552 Engagement dialog) ---------- *@
<partial name="Partials/_audit-engagement-form" />

@* ---------- Add to Plan: pick the plan (546) ----------
   Opened from Audit Definition's "Add to Plan": the audit is known, the
   plan is picked here (Draft / Submitted plans of the organization), or a
   new plan is made first. *@
<dialog id="oaPlPickDialog" style="max-width:560px; width:96%;">
    <form id="oaPlPickForm" method="dialog">
        <div class="pm-dialog-heading">
            <div>
                <h2>Add to Plan</h2>
                <p id="oaPlPickAudit"></p>
            </div>
            <button class="pm-icon-button" type="button" id="oaPlPickClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaPlPickMessage" style="display:none;"></div>
        <label class="pm-field">
            <span>Plan <span class="required">*</span></span>
            <select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPickPlan"></select>
        </label>
        <p class="pm-hint" style="margin:6px 0 0;">Only plans that are still Draft or Submitted can take new audits.</p>
        <div class="pm-dialog-actions">
            <button type="button" id="oaPlPickNew" class="pm-button">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> New Plan
            </button>
            <button type="button" id="oaPlPickCancel" class="pm-button">Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" id="oaPlPickSubmit" class="pm-button primary">Continue</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</dialog>

@* Management dashboard drill-down receiver (414) -- window.__pmDrill. *@
<script src="~/js/Shared/dashboard-drill.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/secure-nav.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';
    const wf = window.__wfCommon;
    if (!wf) { console.error('__wfCommon missing'); return; }

    const API      = '/practice/api/org-assurance';
    const FEATURE  = 'screen.org-assurance-plans';
    // Audit & Assurance dashboard drill-down (414): ?status= is this
    // screen's own Status filter -- plans need nothing more.
    const PL_DRILL = (function () {
        const d = window.__pmDrill ? window.__pmDrill.read() : null;
        return d && d.active ? d : null;
    })();
    const U        = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;

    const state = {
        orgId       : '',
        status      : '',
        planType    : '',
        search      : '',
        page        : 1,
        pageSize    : 25,
        total       : 0,
        // The plan the item dialog and the slot actions work on (set from
        // the plan / slot the action came from).
        selectedPlanId : null,
        selectedPlan   : null,
        expanded    : new Set(),   // open plans (their programmes shown)
        showAll     : new Set(),   // 'planId:programmeId' showing every engagement
        itemsByPlan : {},          // planId -> engagement rows
        // 565: programmes
        methodologies     : [],          // the Planning Methodology master
        programmesByPlan  : {},          // planId -> programme rows
        openProgrammes    : new Set(),   // 'planId:programmeId' showing its engagements
        progForm          : null,        // { planId, programmeId|null } -- the inline form open
        revisionsOpen     : new Set(),   // plans showing their revision history
        revisionsByPlan   : {},
        presetProgrammeId : null,        // Add Engagement from a programme
        plansById   : {},
        statuses    : [],
        planTypes   : [],
        definitions : [],
        itemsById   : {},
        // 546: the audit "Add to Plan" came from (Audit Definition); Add
        // Item opens with it chosen while set.
        presetDefinitionId   : null,
        presetDefinitionName : ''
        // 121: employees[] removed -- picker maintains its own per-role holder cache.
    };

    let openMenuEl      = null;
    let openMenuTrigger = null;

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') boot();

    async function boot() {
        wf.wirePager('oa-plans', function (delta) {
            const next = state.page + delta;
            const maxPage = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(state.total / state.pageSize));
            if (next < 1 || next > maxPage) return;
            state.page = next; reloadPlans();
        });

        const orgs = await wf.loadOrgs();
        if (!orgs.length) {
            wf.unavailable('oaPlUnavailable', 'oaPlUnavailableTitle', 'oaPlUnavailableBody',
                'No accessible organizations', 'Contact your GRAC Admin.');
            return;
        }
        wf.populateOrgSelect('oaPlFilterOrg', orgs);
        // 414: the dashboard's organization wins when it is one of these.
        if (PL_DRILL) window.__pmDrill.preselect('oaPlFilterOrg', PL_DRILL.organizationId);
        state.orgId = document.getElementById('oaPlFilterOrg').value || '';

        const enabled = await wf.checkFeature(FEATURE, state.orgId);
        if (!enabled) {
            wf.unavailable('oaPlUnavailable', 'oaPlUnavailableTitle', 'oaPlUnavailableBody',
                'Audit Plans are not available for this organization.',
                'Ask a GRAC Admin to enable ' + FEATURE + '.');
            return;
        }
        document.getElementById('oaPlRoot').hidden = false;

        try { await Promise.all([loadStatuses(), loadPlanTypes(), loadMethodologies()]); } catch (_) {}
        if (PL_DRILL) {
            if (PL_DRILL.status && window.__pmDrill.preselect('oaPlFilterStatus', PL_DRILL.status))
                state.status = PL_DRILL.status;
            window.__pmDrill.banner('oaPlDrillBanner', PL_DRILL);
        }
        // 121: employees no longer preloaded -- role-holder picker fetches
        // roles + holders lazily when the plan/item dialog opens. Also
        // invalidate any stale role/holder caches so a new org fetches fresh.
        if (window.__roleHolderPicker && typeof window.__roleHolderPicker.invalidateCaches === 'function') {
            window.__roleHolderPicker.invalidateCaches();
        }
        await loadDefinitions(state.orgId);
        wireControls();
        reloadPlans();
        openFromAuditDefinition();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 546: opened from Audit Definition's "Add to Plan". The audit and its
    // organization are in the navigation code; ask which plan to add it to.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function openFromAuditDefinition() {
        const ctx = window.gracSecureNav ? await window.gracSecureNav.context('org-assurance-plans') : null;
        if (!ctx) return;
        if (ctx.error) { alert(ctx.error); return; }
        if (ctx.filterType !== 'AuditDefinition' || !ctx.filterId) return;
        const orgSel = document.getElementById('oaPlFilterOrg');
        const org = ctx.organizationId ? String(ctx.organizationId) : '';
        if (org && org !== state.orgId && Array.prototype.some.call(orgSel.options, function (o) { return o.value === org; })) {
            orgSel.value = org;
            orgSel.dispatchEvent(new Event('change'));
            await loadDefinitions(org);
        }
        const def = state.definitions.find(function (d) { return String(d.definitionId || d.DefinitionId) === String(ctx.filterId); });
        state.presetDefinitionId   = String(ctx.filterId);
        state.presetDefinitionName = def ? ((def.definitionName || def.DefinitionName || '') + ' (' + (def.definitionCode || def.DefinitionCode || '') + ')')
                                         : (ctx.displayCode || '');
        openPickDialog();
    }

    async function openPickDialog() {
        const msg = document.getElementById('oaPlPickMessage');
        msg.style.display = 'none'; msg.textContent = '';
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickAudit').textContent = 'Audit: ' + state.presetDefinitionName;
        const sel = document.getElementById('oaPlPickPlan');
        sel.innerHTML = '<option value="">Loading plans...</option>';
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickDialog').showModal();
        try {
            const qs = new URLSearchParams();
            qs.set('organizationId', state.orgId);
            qs.set('page', '1'); qs.set('pageSize', '200');
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plans?' + qs.toString()), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const payload = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            const rows = ((payload && (payload.rows || payload.Rows)) || []).filter(function (p) {
                const st = p.statusCode || p.StatusCode || '';
                return st === 'Draft' || st === 'Submitted';
            });
            rows.forEach(function (p) { state.plansById[String(p.planId || p.PlanId)] = p; });
            sel.innerHTML = rows.length
                ? '<option value="">-- pick a plan --</option>'
                : '<option value="">No Draft or Submitted plan. Use New Plan.</option>';
            rows.forEach(function (p) {
                const opt = document.createElement('option');
                opt.value = String(p.planId || p.PlanId);
                opt.textContent = (p.planName || p.PlanName || '') + ' (' + (p.planCode || p.PlanCode || '') + ')'
                    + '  --  ' + periodLabel(p.periodFrom || p.PeriodFrom, p.periodTo || p.PeriodTo);
                sel.appendChild(opt);
            });
        } catch (err) {
            sel.innerHTML = '<option value="">Failed to load plans</option>';
        }
    }
    function closePickDialog() { document.getElementById('oaPlPickDialog').close(); }
    // The plan is chosen: show it and open Add Item with the audit chosen.
    function continueWithPlan(planId) {
        closePickDialog();
        selectPlan(Number(planId));
        openItemDialog(null);
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Wiring
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function wireControls() {
        document.getElementById('oaPlFilterOrg').addEventListener('change', async function (e) {
            state.orgId          = e.target.value || '';
            state.page           = 1;
            state.selectedPlanId = null;
            state.selectedPlan   = null;
            state.expanded.clear(); state.showAll.clear(); state.itemsByPlan = {};
            state.programmesByPlan = {}; state.openProgrammes.clear(); state.progForm = null;   // 565
            state.revisionsOpen.clear(); state.revisionsByPlan = {};
            // 121: employees no longer preloaded -- role-holder picker fetches
        // roles + holders lazily when the plan/item dialog opens. Also
        // invalidate any stale role/holder caches so a new org fetches fresh.
        if (window.__roleHolderPicker && typeof window.__roleHolderPicker.invalidateCaches === 'function') {
            window.__roleHolderPicker.invalidateCaches();
        }
        await loadDefinitions(state.orgId);
            reloadPlans();
        });
        document.getElementById('oaPlFilterStatus').addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            state.status = e.target.value || ''; state.page = 1; reloadPlans();
        });
        document.getElementById('oaPlFilterType').addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            state.planType = e.target.value || ''; state.page = 1; reloadPlans();
        });
        document.getElementById('oaPlSearch').addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            state.search = e.target.value || ''; state.page = 1;
            clearTimeout(window.__oaPlSearchTimer);
            window.__oaPlSearchTimer = setTimeout(reloadPlans, 250);
        });
        document.getElementById('oaPlRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', function () { reloadPlans(); });
        document.getElementById('oaPlAddBtn').addEventListener('click',    function () { openPlanDialog(null); });

        document.getElementById('oaPlPlanClose').addEventListener('click', closePlanDialog);
        document.getElementById('oaPlPlanCancel').addEventListener('click', closePlanDialog);
        document.getElementById('oaPlPlanForm').addEventListener('submit', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); savePlan(); });

        // 546: Add to Plan's plan picker.
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickClose').addEventListener('click', closePickDialog);
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickCancel').addEventListener('click', closePickDialog);
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickNew').addEventListener('click', function () {
            closePickDialog();
            openPlanDialog(null);
        });
        document.getElementById('oaPlPickForm').addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const v = document.getElementById('oaPlPickPlan').value;
            if (!v) {
                const msg = document.getElementById('oaPlPickMessage');
                msg.style.display = 'block'; msg.textContent = 'Pick a plan, or use New Plan.';
                return;
            }
            continueWithPlan(v);
        });

        // 566: the engagement form and View Scope wire themselves
        // (js/Shared/audit-engagement-form.js).

        wireRowMenus();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Lookups
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function loadStatuses() {
        const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plan-statuses'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
        if (!r.ok) return;
        const b = await r.json();
        state.statuses = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        const sel = document.getElementById('oaPlFilterStatus');
        for (const s of state.statuses) {
            const opt = document.createElement('option');
            opt.value = s.statusCode || s.StatusCode;
            opt.textContent = s.statusName || s.StatusName;
            sel.appendChild(opt);
        }
    }
    async function loadPlanTypes() {
        const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plan-types'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
        if (!r.ok) return;
        const b = await r.json();
        state.planTypes = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        const filter = document.getElementById('oaPlFilterType');
        for (const t of state.planTypes) {
            const opt = document.createElement('option');
            opt.value = t.planTypeCode || t.PlanTypeCode;
            opt.textContent = t.planTypeName || t.PlanTypeName;
            filter.appendChild(opt);
        }
    }
    // 565: the Planning Methodology master (a programme picks one).
    async function loadMethodologies() {
        const r = await fetch(U(API + '/planning-methodologies'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
        if (!r.ok) return;
        const b = await r.json();
        state.methodologies = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
    }
    async function loadDefinitions(orgId) {
        if (!orgId) { state.definitions = []; return; }
        try {
            const qs = new URLSearchParams();
            qs.set('organizationId', orgId);
            qs.set('page', '1'); qs.set('pageSize', '500');
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/definitions?' + qs.toString()), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) { state.definitions = []; return; }
            const payload = await r.json();
            state.definitions = payload.rows || payload.Rows || [];
        } catch (_) { state.definitions = []; }
    }
    // 121 -- loadEmployees retired.
    // Owner + Auditor pickers use window.__roleHolderPicker which fetches
    // roles + per-role holders lazily on dialog open.

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Plans list
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function reloadPlans() {
        const body = document.getElementById('oaPlPlanBody');
        if (!state.orgId) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load plans.</td></tr>';
            wf.updatePager('oa-plans', { pageNumber: 1, totalCount: 0, pageSize: 1 });
            return;
        }
        body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        try {
            const qs = new URLSearchParams();
            qs.set('organizationId', state.orgId);
            if (state.status)   qs.set('statusCode', state.status);
            if (state.planType) qs.set('planType',   state.planType);
            if (state.search)   qs.set('search',     state.search);
            qs.set('page',     String(state.page));
            qs.set('pageSize', String(state.pageSize));
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plans?' + qs.toString()), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) { body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">HTTP ' + r.status + '</td></tr>'; return; }
            const payload = await r.json();
            state.total = Number(payload.totalCount || payload.TotalCount || 0);
            const rows  = payload.rows || payload.Rows || [];
            renderPlansRows(rows);
            wf.updatePager('oa-plans', {
                pageNumber : state.page,
                totalCount : state.total,
                pageSize   : state.pageSize
            });
        } catch (err) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">Failed to load: ' + wf.escape(err.message || err) + '</td></tr>';
        }
    }

    function renderPlansRows(rows) {
        const body = document.getElementById('oaPlPlanBody');
        state.plansById = {};
        if (!rows.length) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">No plans yet. Click "Add Plan" to create one.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        body.innerHTML = rows.map(function (row) {
            const id     = row.planId  || row.PlanId;
            const code   = row.planCode|| row.PlanCode || '';
            const name   = row.planName|| row.PlanName || '';
            const type   = planTypeName(row.planType || row.PlanType || '');
            const period = periodLabel(row.periodFrom || row.PeriodFrom, row.periodTo || row.PeriodTo);
            const owner  = wf.personWithRole(row.ownerDisplayName || row.OwnerDisplayName, row.ownerRoleName || row.OwnerRoleName);
            const items  = row.itemCount || row.ItemCount || 0;
            // 565: programmes, and planned vs actual.
            const progs  = row.programmeCount ?? row.ProgrammeCount ?? 0;
            const inProg = row.engagementInProgressCount ?? row.EngagementInProgressCount ?? 0;
            const done   = row.engagementCompletedCount  ?? row.EngagementCompletedCount  ?? 0;
            const stCode = row.statusCode || row.StatusCode || '';
            const stName = row.statusName || row.StatusName || '';
            if (id != null) state.plansById[String(id)] = row;
            const open = state.expanded.has(String(id));
            // The Task Board's sub-task chevron (.task-tree-toggle); a row
            // click does the same.
            return '<tr class="pm-row-clickable oa-pl-plan' + (open ? ' oa-pl-open is-selected' : '') + '" data-id="' + id + '" data-status="' + wf.escape(stCode) + '">'
                 + '<td><span class="task-tree-cell">'
                 + '<button type="button" class="task-tree-toggle' + (open ? ' is-open' : '') + '" data-plan-toggle="' + id + '"'
                 + ' aria-expanded="' + (open ? 'true' : 'false') + '" title="Show the programmes">'
                 + '<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>'
                 + '<span class="visually-hidden">Show the programmes</span></button>'
                 + '<span>' + wf.escape(code) + '</span></span></td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(name) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(type) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(period) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(owner) + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(String(progs)) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(plannedVsActual(items, inProg, done)) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.badge(stName) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + trigger(id, 'plan') + '</td>'
                 + '</tr>';
        }).join('');

        // Plans that were open stay open, with their slots read again.
        state.expanded.forEach(function (pid) {
            if (state.plansById[pid]) loadItems(pid); else state.expanded.delete(pid);
        });
    }

    // Chevron or row click: open / close the plan's slots.
    document.getElementById('oaPlPlanBody').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger, .pm-action-menu, .oa-pl-items, a')) return;
        const tr = e.target.closest('tr.oa-pl-plan[data-id]');
        if (tr) togglePlan(tr.getAttribute('data-id'));
    });

    function planRow(planId) {
        return document.querySelector('#oaPlPlanBody tr.oa-pl-plan[data-id="' + String(planId) + '"]');
    }
    function setToggle(planId, open) {
        const btn = document.querySelector('#oaPlPlanBody [data-plan-toggle="' + String(planId) + '"]');
        const row = planRow(planId);
        if (row) { row.classList.toggle('oa-pl-open', open); row.classList.toggle('is-selected', open); }
        if (!btn) return;
        btn.classList.toggle('is-open', open);
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
    }
    function togglePlan(planId) {
        const pid = String(planId);
        if (state.expanded.has(pid)) {
            state.expanded.delete(pid);
            Array.from(state.showAll).forEach(function (k) { if (k.split(':')[0] === pid) state.showAll.delete(k); });   // 565
            const child = document.querySelector('#oaPlPlanBody tr.oa-pl-items-row[data-plan="' + pid + '"]');
            if (child) child.remove();
            setToggle(pid, false);
            return;
        }
        state.expanded.add(pid);
        setToggle(pid, true);
        loadItems(pid);
    }

    // Opens the plan (if it is not open) and makes it the target of the
    // item dialog -- Add to Plan, and the plan's own Add Item.
    function selectPlan(planId) {
        state.selectedPlanId = Number(planId);
        state.selectedPlan   = state.plansById[String(planId)] || null;
        if (!state.expanded.has(String(planId)) && planRow(planId)) togglePlan(planId);
    }

    // 546: slots change only while the plan is Draft or Submitted.
    function planStatus(planId) {
        const row = state.plansById[String(planId)]
                 || (state.selectedPlan && String(state.selectedPlan.planId || state.selectedPlan.PlanId) === String(planId) ? state.selectedPlan : {})
                 || {};
        return row.statusCode || row.StatusCode || '';
    }
    function selectedPlanStatus() { return planStatus(state.selectedPlanId); }
    function planEditable(planId) {
        const st = planStatus(planId != null ? planId : state.selectedPlanId);
        return st === 'Draft' || st === 'Submitted';
    }

    // The child row under a plan: its slots in their own small table.
    function itemsRow(planId) {
        const pid = String(planId);
        let child = document.querySelector('#oaPlPlanBody tr.oa-pl-items-row[data-plan="' + pid + '"]');
        if (!child) {
            const parent = planRow(pid);
            if (!parent) return null;
            child = document.createElement('tr');
            child.className = 'oa-pl-items-row is-selected';
            child.setAttribute('data-plan', pid);
            child.innerHTML = '<td colspan="9"><div class="oa-pl-items"></div></td>';
            parent.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', child);
        }
        return child.querySelector('.oa-pl-items');
    }

    const SLOT_CAP = 20;
    async function loadItems(planId) {
        const pid  = String(planId);
        const host = itemsRow(pid);
        if (!host || !state.orgId) return;
        if (!state.itemsByPlan[pid]) host.innerHTML = '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:0;">Loading programmes...</p>';
        try {
            // 565: the plan's programmes and its engagements.
            const q = '?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId);
            const both = await Promise.all([
                fetch(U(API + '/plans/' + pid + '/items' + q), { credentials: 'same-origin' }),
                fetch(U(API + '/plans/' + pid + '/programmes' + q), { credentials: 'same-origin' })
            ]);
            if (!both[0].ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + both[0].status);
            if (!both[1].ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + both[1].status);
            const b = await both[0].json();
            const rows = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
            const pb = await both[1].json();
            state.programmesByPlan[pid] = (pb && (pb.data || pb.Data)) || [];
            state.itemsByPlan[pid] = rows;
            rows.forEach(function (row) { state.itemsById[String(row.planItemId || row.PlanItemId)] = row; });
            if (state.revisionsOpen.has(pid)) await loadRevisions(pid);
            renderItems(pid);
        } catch (err) {
            host.innerHTML = '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:0;">Programmes could not be loaded: ' + wf.escape(err.message || err) + '</p>';
        }
    }
    // Re-reads one plan's slots (after a change) and the list's counts.
    function reloadItems(planId) {
        const pid = String(planId != null ? planId : state.selectedPlanId);
        if (!state.expanded.has(pid)) { state.expanded.add(pid); setToggle(pid, true); }
        return loadItems(pid);
    }

    // 565: the child row under a plan -- a facts line, its PROGRAMMES (each
    // opens its engagements in a row under it), the inline programme form,
    // and the revision history.
    function renderItems(planId) {
        const pid  = String(planId);
        const host = itemsRow(pid);
        if (!host) return;
        const plan  = state.plansById[pid] || {};
        const progs = state.programmesByPlan[pid] || [];
        const all   = state.itemsByPlan[pid] || [];
        const editable = planEditable(pid);
        const facts = [
            'Version ' + (plan.version ?? plan.Version ?? 1),
            plan.financialYear || plan.FinancialYear || '',
            (plan.methodologies || plan.Methodologies) ? 'Methodologies: ' + (plan.methodologies || plan.Methodologies) : '',
            'Planned vs actual: ' + plannedVsActual(plan.itemCount ?? plan.ItemCount ?? all.length,
                plan.engagementInProgressCount ?? plan.EngagementInProgressCount ?? 0,
                plan.engagementCompletedCount  ?? plan.EngagementCompletedCount  ?? 0)
        ].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');
        const version = Number(plan.version ?? plan.Version ?? 1);
        const revLink = version > 1
            ? '<a href="#" class="oa-pl-more" data-revisions="' + pid + '">'
              + (state.revisionsOpen.has(pid) ? 'Hide' : 'Show') + ' revision history</a>' : '';
        const addProg = editable && !(state.progForm && String(state.progForm.planId) === pid && state.progForm.programmeId == null)
            ? '<a href="#" class="oa-pl-add" data-add-programme="' + pid + '"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add Programme</a>' : '';
        const newForm = state.progForm && String(state.progForm.planId) === pid && state.progForm.programmeId == null
            ? programmeFormRow(pid, null) : '';

        let html = '<p class="oa-pl-plan-facts">' + wf.escape(facts) + '</p>';
        if (!progs.length && !newForm) {
            html += '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:0 0 6px;">No programmes yet. A plan groups its engagements into programmes; add one first.'
                  + (editable ? '' : ' Programmes can be added only while the plan is Draft or Submitted.') + '</p>';
        } else {
            html += '<div class="pm-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>'
                  + '<th>Code</th><th>Programme</th><th>Planning Methodology</th><th>Owner</th><th>Engagements</th><th style="width:70px;"></th>'
                  + '</tr></thead><tbody>'
                  + progs.map(function (g) {
                        const gid  = String(g.programmeId ?? g.ProgrammeId);
                        const key  = pid + ':' + gid;
                        const open = state.openProgrammes.has(key);
                        if (state.progForm && String(state.progForm.planId) === pid && String(state.progForm.programmeId) === gid)
                            return programmeFormRow(pid, g);
                        const owner = wf.personWithRole(g.ownerDisplayName || g.OwnerDisplayName, g.ownerRoleName || g.OwnerRoleName);
                        return '<tr class="pm-row-clickable' + (open ? ' oa-pl-prog-open' : '') + '" data-programme="' + gid + '" data-plan="' + pid + '">'
                             + '<td><span class="task-tree-cell">'
                             + '<button type="button" class="task-tree-toggle' + (open ? ' is-open' : '') + '" aria-expanded="' + (open ? 'true' : 'false') + '" title="Show the engagements">'
                             + '<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">Show the engagements</span></button>'
                             + '<span>' + wf.escape(g.programmeCode || g.ProgrammeCode || '') + '</span></span></td>'
                             + '<td>' + wf.escape(g.programmeName || g.ProgrammeName || '') + '</td>'
                             + '<td>' + wf.escape(g.methodologyName || g.MethodologyName || 'Not set') + '</td>'
                             + '<td>' + wf.escape(owner) + '</td>'
                             + '<td>' + wf.escape(plannedVsActual(g.engagementCount ?? g.EngagementCount ?? 0,
                                    g.engagementInProgressCount ?? g.EngagementInProgressCount ?? 0,
                                    g.engagementCompletedCount ?? g.EngagementCompletedCount ?? 0)) + '</td>'
                             + '<td>' + trigger(gid, 'programme') + '</td>'
                             + '</tr>'
                             + (open ? '<tr class="oa-pl-prog-items"><td colspan="6">' + engagementsHtml(pid, gid) + '</td></tr>' : '');
                    }).join('')
                  + newForm
                  + '</tbody></table></div>';
        }
        // Engagements without a programme (only before 565's backfill ran).
        const loose = all.filter(function (r) { return (r.programmeId ?? r.ProgrammeId) == null; });
        if (loose.length && progs.length) html += '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:8px 0 4px;">Not in a programme yet (edit to pick one):</p>' + engagementsHtml(pid, null);
        else if (loose.length) html += engagementsHtml(pid, null);
        html += '<div class="oa-pl-items-foot">' + addProg + revLink + '</div>';
        if (state.revisionsOpen.has(pid)) html += revisionsHtml(pid);
        host.innerHTML = html;
        if (state.progForm && String(state.progForm.planId) === pid) attachProgrammeOwner();
    }

    // "5 planned, 1 in progress, 2 completed" -- planned vs actual.
    function plannedVsActual(total, inProg, done) {
        const t = Number(total) || 0, p = Number(inProg) || 0, d = Number(done) || 0;
        return t + ' planned' + (p ? ', ' + p + ' in progress' : '') + (d ? ', ' + d + ' completed' : '');
    }

    // A programme's engagements (programmeId null: those without one) --
    // the engagement grid of 552, unchanged.
    function engagementsHtml(planId, programmeId) {
        const pid  = String(planId);
        const key  = pid + ':' + (programmeId == null ? '' : String(programmeId));
        const all  = (state.itemsByPlan[pid] || []).filter(function (r) {
            const g = r.programmeId ?? r.ProgrammeId;
            return programmeId == null ? g == null : String(g) === String(programmeId);
        });
        const shown = state.showAll.has(key) ? all : all.slice(0, SLOT_CAP);
        const addLink = planEditable(pid) && programmeId != null
            ? '<a href="#" class="oa-pl-add" data-add-item="' + pid + '" data-add-programme-item="' + wf.escape(String(programmeId)) + '"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add Engagement</a>'
            : '';
        if (!all.length) {
            return '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:0 0 6px;">No engagements in this programme yet.'
                + (planEditable(pid) ? '' : ' Engagements can be added only while the plan is Draft or Submitted.') + '</p>' + addLink;
        }
        return '<div class="pm-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>'
            + '<th style="width:70px;">Order</th><th>Engagement</th><th>Audits</th><th>Scheduled</th><th>Auditor</th>'
            + '<th>Team / Department</th><th>Status</th><th style="width:70px;"></th>'
            + '</tr></thead><tbody>'
            + shown.map(function (row) {
                const id       = row.planItemId  || row.PlanItemId;
                const order    = row.itemOrder ?? row.ItemOrder ?? '';
                // 552: the engagement and its audits.
                const engName  = row.engagementName || row.EngagementName || row.definitionName || row.DefinitionName || '';
                const engCode  = row.engagementCode || row.EngagementCode || '';
                const audits   = row.definitionCodes || row.DefinitionCodes || row.definitionCode || row.DefinitionCode || '';
                const from     = onlyDate(row.scheduledFrom || row.ScheduledFrom);
                const to       = onlyDate(row.scheduledTo   || row.ScheduledTo);
                const sched    = from || to ? (from + (to ? ' - ' + to : '')) : '';
                // 121 hybrid role+employee auditor -- composite label with graceful fallback.
                const auRole   = row.assignedAuditorRoleName || row.AssignedAuditorRoleName || '';
                const auEmp    = row.assignedAuditorName     || row.AssignedAuditorName     || '';
                const auditor  = (auRole && auEmp) ? (auRole + ' (' + auEmp + ')') : (auRole || auEmp);
                const team     = row.assignedTeamName       || row.AssignedTeamName       || '';
                const dept     = row.assignedDepartmentName || row.AssignedDepartmentName || '';
                const teamDept = [team, dept].filter(Boolean).join(' / ');
                return '<tr data-id="' + id + '" data-plan="' + pid + '">'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(String(order)) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(engName) + (engCode ? ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">(' + wf.escape(engCode) + ')</span>' : '') + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(audits) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(sched) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(auditor) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(teamDept) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + slotStatusHtml(row) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + trigger(id, 'item') + '</td>'
                     + '</tr>';
            }).join('')
            + '</tbody></table></div>'
            + '<div class="oa-pl-items-foot">' + addLink
            + (all.length > shown.length
                ? '<a href="#" class="oa-pl-more" data-show-all="' + wf.escape(key) + '">Show all ' + all.length + ' engagements</a>' : '')
            + '</div>';
    }

    // The inline programme form (565, no popups): a row of the programme
    // table -- for a new programme at the bottom, for an edit in place.
    function programmeFormRow(planId, g) {
        const v = function (a, b) { return g ? (g[a] ?? g[b] ?? '') : ''; };
        const mid = String(v('planningMethodologyId', 'PlanningMethodologyId'));
        const opts = '<option value="">-- select --</option>' + state.methodologies.map(function (m) {
            const id = String(m.id ?? m.Id);
            return '<option value="' + wf.escape(id) + '"' + (id === mid ? ' selected' : '') + '>' + wf.escape(m.name || m.Name || '') + '</option>';
        }).join('');
        return '<tr class="oa-pl-prog-form" data-prog-form="' + wf.escape(String(planId)) + '"><td colspan="6">'
             + '<div class="pm-message" id="oaPlPgMessage" style="display:none; margin-bottom:8px;"></div>'
             + '<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,2fr) minmax(0,1fr) 90px; gap:10px; align-items:start;">'
             +   '<label class="pm-field" style="min-width:0;"><span>Programme <span class="required">*</span></span>'
             +     '<input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgName" type="text" maxlength="240" value="' + wf.escape(v('programmeName', 'ProgrammeName'))
             +     '" placeholder="e.g. Information Systems Audit Programme" /></label>'
             +   '<label class="pm-field" style="min-width:0;"><span>Planning Methodology <span class="required">*</span></span>'
             +     '<select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgMethod">' + opts + '</select></label>'
             +   '<label class="pm-field" style="min-width:0;"><span>Order</span>'
             +     '<input class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgOrder" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="' + wf.escape(String(v('displayOrder', 'DisplayOrder'))) + '" /></label>'
             + '</div>'
             + '<div class="pm-field" style="min-width:0; margin-top:10px;"><span>Owner</span>'
             +   '<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:6px; margin-top:2px;">'
             +     '<select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgOwnerRole" style="min-width:0;" aria-label="Owner Role"><option value="">Loading roles...</option></select>'
             +     '<select class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgOwner" style="min-width:0;" aria-label="Owner Employee"><option value="">-- pick a role first --</option></select>'
             +   '</div></div>'
             + '<label class="pm-field" style="margin-top:10px;"><span>Objective</span>'
             +   '<textarea class="pm-input" id="oaPlPgObjective" rows="2" maxlength="4000">' + wf.escape(v('objective', 'Objective')) + '</textarea></label>'
             + '<div class="pm-dialog-actions">'
             +   '<button type="button" class="pm-button" data-prog-cancel>Cancel</button>'
             +   '<button type="button" class="pm-button primary" data-prog-save>Save Programme</button>'
             + '</div>'
             + '</td></tr>';
    }
    // The form's owner pickers (121 role + current holder).
    function attachProgrammeOwner() {
        if (!state.orgId || !window.__roleHolderPicker || !document.getElementById('oaPlPgOwnerRole')) return;
        const pid = String(state.progForm.planId);
        const g = (state.programmesByPlan[pid] || []).find(function (x) {
            return String(x.programmeId ?? x.ProgrammeId) === String(state.progForm.programmeId);
        }) || {};
        window.__roleHolderPicker.attach({
            organizationId     : Number(state.orgId),
            roleSelectId       : 'oaPlPgOwnerRole',
            employeeSelectId   : 'oaPlPgOwner',
            initialRoleId      : g.ownerRoleId      ?? g.OwnerRoleId,
            initialRoleName    : g.ownerRoleName    || g.OwnerRoleName,
            initialEmployeeId  : g.ownerEmployeeId  ?? g.OwnerEmployeeId,
            initialEmployeeName: g.ownerDisplayName || g.OwnerDisplayName,
            allowEmpty         : true
        }).catch(function () { /* soft-fail, as the plan owner */ });
    }
    function openProgrammeForm(planId, programmeId) {
        state.progForm = { planId: String(planId), programmeId: programmeId == null ? null : String(programmeId) };
        if (!state.expanded.has(String(planId))) { state.expanded.add(String(planId)); setToggle(planId, true); loadItems(planId); return; }
        renderItems(planId);
    }
    async function saveProgramme() {
        const f = state.progForm;
        if (!f) return;
        const msg = function (t) {
            const el = document.getElementById('oaPlPgMessage');
            if (!el) return;
            el.style.display = t ? 'block' : 'none';
            el.style.background = 'var(--danger-100)'; el.style.color = 'var(--danger-700)';
            el.textContent = t || '';
        };
        const name = document.getElementById('oaPlPgName').value.trim();
        const method = document.getElementById('oaPlPgMethod').value;
        if (!name) { msg('The programme needs a name.'); return; }
        if (!method) { msg('Pick the planning methodology.'); return; }
        const owner = (window.__roleHolderPicker && typeof window.__roleHolderPicker.readState === 'function')
            ? window.__roleHolderPicker.readState('oaPlPgOwnerRole', 'oaPlPgOwner')
            : { roleId: null, roleName: null, employeeId: null, employeeName: null };
        const order = document.getElementById('oaPlPgOrder').value;
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plan-programmes'), {
                method: 'POST', credentials: 'same-origin',
                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body: JSON.stringify({
                    organizationId        : Number(state.orgId),
                    planId                : Number(f.planId),
                    programmeId           : f.programmeId != null ? Number(f.programmeId) : null,
                    programmeName         : name,
                    objective             : document.getElementById('oaPlPgObjective').value.trim() || null,
                    planningMethodologyId : Number(method),
                    ownerRoleId           : owner.roleId       || null,
                    ownerRoleName         : owner.roleName     || null,
                    ownerEmployeeId       : owner.employeeId   || null,
                    ownerDisplayName      : owner.employeeName || null,
                    displayOrder          : order ? Number(order) : null,
                    actor                 : null
                })
            });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) { msg((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status)); return; }
            state.progForm = null;
            reloadPlans();   // counts and methodologies; the open plan re-reads its programmes
        } catch (err) { msg(err.message || String(err)); }
    }
    async function deleteProgramme(planId, programmeId) {
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm('Remove this programme from the plan? It must have no engagements.',
              { type: 'warning', title: 'Remove programme', confirmText: 'Remove' })) return;
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plans/' + encodeURIComponent(planId) + '/programmes/' + encodeURIComponent(programmeId)
                                    + '?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)), { method: 'DELETE', credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) { await window.gracUi.alert((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status), { type: 'error' }); return; }
            state.openProgrammes.delete(String(planId) + ':' + String(programmeId));
            reloadPlans();
        } catch (err) { await window.gracUi.alert(err.message || String(err), { type: 'error' }); }
    }

    // 565: plan revision -- reason, back to Draft, version + 1.
    async function revisePlan(planId) {
        // gracUi.promptRequired: a blank reason asks again; Cancel is null.
        const reason = await window.gracUi.promptRequired('Why is the plan being revised? It goes back to Draft (version + 1) and must be submitted and approved again. Running audits continue.',
            { title: 'Revise plan', confirmText: 'Revise', multiline: true });
        if (reason === null) return;
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plans/' + encodeURIComponent(planId) + '/revise'), {
                method: 'POST', credentials: 'same-origin',
                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body: JSON.stringify({ organizationId: Number(state.orgId), planId: Number(planId), reason: String(reason).trim(), actor: null })
            });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) { await window.gracUi.alert((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status), { type: 'error' }); return; }
            state.revisionsByPlan[String(planId)] = null;
            state.expanded.add(String(planId));
            reloadPlans();
        } catch (err) { await window.gracUi.alert(err.message || String(err), { type: 'error' }); }
    }
    async function loadRevisions(planId) {
        const pid = String(planId);
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/plans/' + pid + '/revisions?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const b = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            state.revisionsByPlan[pid] = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        } catch (_) { state.revisionsByPlan[pid] = []; }
    }
    function revisionsHtml(planId) {
        const rows = state.revisionsByPlan[String(planId)] || [];
        if (!rows.length) return '<p class="pm-hint" style="margin:8px 0 0;">No revisions recorded.</p>';
        return '<div class="pm-table-wrap" style="margin-top:8px;"><table><thead><tr>'
             + '<th>Version</th><th>Was</th><th>Reason</th><th>Revised by</th><th>On</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
             + rows.map(function (x) {
                   return '<tr><td>' + wf.escape(String(x.fromVersion ?? x.FromVersion) + ' → ' + String(x.toVersion ?? x.ToVersion)) + '</td>'
                        + '<td>' + wf.escape(x.fromStatusCode || x.FromStatusCode || '') + '</td>'
                        + '<td>' + wf.escape(x.reason || x.Reason || '') + '</td>'
                        + '<td>' + wf.escape(x.revisedBy || x.RevisedBy || '') + '</td>'
                        + '<td>' + wf.escape(onlyDate(x.revisedDt || x.RevisedDt)) + '</td></tr>';
               }).join('')
             + '</tbody></table></div>';
    }

    // 565: programme rows open / close their engagements; the inline form,
    // Add Programme and the revision history.
    document.getElementById('oaPlPlanBody').addEventListener('click', async function (e) {
        if (e.target.closest('[data-prog-save]'))   { e.preventDefault(); saveProgramme(); return; }
        if (e.target.closest('[data-prog-cancel]')) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const pid = state.progForm && state.progForm.planId;
            state.progForm = null;
            if (pid) renderItems(pid);
            return;
        }
        const addProg = e.target.closest('[data-add-programme]');
        if (addProg) { e.preventDefault(); openProgrammeForm(addProg.getAttribute('data-add-programme'), null); return; }
        const rev = e.target.closest('[data-revisions]');
        if (rev) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const pid = rev.getAttribute('data-revisions');
            if (state.revisionsOpen.has(pid)) state.revisionsOpen.delete(pid);
            else { state.revisionsOpen.add(pid); await loadRevisions(pid); }
            renderItems(pid);
            return;
        }
        if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger, .pm-action-menu, a, input, select, textarea, button:not(.task-tree-toggle)')) return;
        const tr = e.target.closest('tr[data-programme]');
        if (!tr) return;
        const key = tr.getAttribute('data-plan') + ':' + tr.getAttribute('data-programme');
        if (state.openProgrammes.has(key)) state.openProgrammes.delete(key); else state.openProgrammes.add(key);
        renderItems(tr.getAttribute('data-plan'));
    });

    // Add Item / Show all inside a plan's child row.
    document.getElementById('oaPlPlanBody').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        const add = e.target.closest('[data-add-item]');
        if (add) {
            e.preventDefault();
            state.selectedPlanId = Number(add.getAttribute('data-add-item'));
            state.selectedPlan   = state.plansById[String(state.selectedPlanId)] || null;
            state.presetProgrammeId = add.getAttribute('data-add-programme-item');   // 565
            openItemDialog(null);
            return;
        }
        const more = e.target.closest('[data-show-all]');
        if (more) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const key = more.getAttribute('data-show-all');   // 565: 'planId:programmeId'
            state.showAll.add(key);
            renderItems(key.split(':')[0]);
        }
    });

